        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 24 at 3:42PM CDT until September 24 at 4:30PM CDT by NWS Norman OK</headline>
        <description>SVROUN

The National Weather Service in Norman has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
North central Ellis County in northwestern Oklahoma...
Northwestern Woods County in northwestern Oklahoma...
Southeastern Harper County in northwestern Oklahoma...
Northern Woodward County in northwestern Oklahoma...

* Until 430 PM CDT.

* At 342 PM CDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line
extending from 5 miles south of Buffalo to 5 miles north of Fargo,
moving east at 35 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage
to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Buffalo, Fort Supply, Freedom, Alabaster Caverns State Park,
Selman, and Camp Houston.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
